{{wikipedia|cleric}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|lang=la|clericus|clēricus}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|lang=grc|κληρικός|tr=klērikos}}, from {{term|lang=grc|κλῆρος|tr=klēros||a casting lots, drawing lots}}, (Europe; many officers at Athens obtained their offices by lot, as opposed to election [''Liddell and Scott'']), from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|kald-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|klād-||timber, log|lang=ine-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{recons|kola-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|klā-||to beat, hew, break, destroy, kill|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/klɛɹɪk/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/klErIk/}}
* {{rhymes|ɛɹɪk}}

